# .uis.extend/neko-exposure.yaml
#
# HOW THIS INSTALLATION EXPOSES NEKO.
#
# ⚠️ YOU DO NOT NEED TO EDIT THIS FILE. Every value below is optional and the
# defaults work on any cluster. It exists for the one thing that cannot be
# discovered: a remote overlay address.
#
# THE MODEL
#
#   LAN is the base.  A plain LoadBalancer on the node's own address. Works on
#                     Rancher Desktop, on Proxmox, in the cloud — no Tailscale
#                     operator, no CNI-specific feature. Agents, other services
#                     and the test harness all reach neko this way.
#   Tailnet is an     Added only where the Tailscale operator exists. It never
#   overlay.          replaces the LAN path, so the service keeps working
#                     without it.
#
# WHY THE ADDRESS MATTERS AT ALL
#
# neko's web view is plain HTTP and reaches users through Traefik like anything
# else. Its *media* cannot: WebRTC needs raw TCP, and neko advertises addresses
# to the viewer through ICE. The browser then connects to exactly those. So an
# advertised address must be one the VIEWER can reach.
#
# Get it wrong and the failure is quiet: the page loads, the pod is Ready,
# /health is 200, and the screen stays black.
#
# The node's InternalIP is discovered automatically and always advertised, which
# is why the default needs no editing.

# --- optional: the tailnet overlay ---
# Adds a SECOND Service via the Tailscale operator for the web view, so a human
# can reach neko remotely. The web view is password-gated by neko itself, so
# both paths are safe.
# ⚠️ CDP is deliberately NOT put on the overlay — the token is its guard, and
# the fewer places it is reachable, the better.
# tailnet_overlay: false
# hostname: "neko"

# --- optional: extra addresses to advertise for MEDIA ---
# Only needed for viewers arriving over an overlay. A tailnet IP cannot be
# discovered before its LoadBalancer exists, so it has to be stated here — the
# deploy prints the address to use and re-running picks it up.
# Without this, a remote viewer gets the page and a black screen.
# extra_advertise_addresses: ["100.97.5.40"]

# --- advanced ---
# The port neko listens on for muxed WebRTC TCP, and advertises. These are the
# same number by necessity: ICE offers the port neko listens on, so a Service
# that renumbered it would advertise a port the viewer cannot open.
# tcpmux_port: 32816
